In North America, clearly defining the Scope of Work is a crucial issue. Design documents must precisely delineate the work content, such as whether fire protection systems are included. These terms need to be specified in detail when signing contracts.

Optimizing designs requires considering multiple factors:

Designs should ensure constructability to avoid on-site implementation issues;

System performance should be reasonably efficient while meeting energy-saving requirements;

Ease of future operation and maintenance must be considered;

Among various design options, choose those that both reduce costs and accelerate construction progress.

Industry experts are well aware of how to define design scope: it’s about clarifying the specific content and boundaries of design work.

